{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '49,59p' .pose/roadmaps/pose-shared-runtime.md; sed -n '80,140p' .pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md; rg -n 'TODO|FIXME|stub|panic\\\\(' pose-mcp/internal/pose/{bounded_cache.go,cache_size.go,delivery_integrity_cache.go,design_delta.go,test_catalog.go,git_spawn_cache.go}; sed -n '355,390p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/bounded_cache.go; sed -n '100,135p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/graph_view_isolation_test.go; sed -n '230,245p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/graph_cache_measure_test.go\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '49,59p' .pose/roadmaps/pose-shared-runtime.md; sed -n '80,140p' .pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md; rg -n 'TODO|FIXME|stub|panic\\\\(' pose-mcp/internal/pose/{bounded_cache.go,cache_size.go,delivery_integrity_cache.go,design_delta.go,test_catalog.go,git_spawn_cache.go}; sed -n '355,390p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/bounded_cache.go; sed -n '100,135p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/graph_view_isolation_test.go; sed -n '230,245p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/graph_cache_measure_test.go\"","aggregated_output":"## Milestone: bounded-graph-caches\n- after: spec:pose-index-generation-integrity, spec:pose-governance-read-view-generation, spec:pose-delivery-integrity-index-compaction\n- target_start:\n- target_due:\n- specs: pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches\n\n**Exit gate:** B33 conserva grafo/filtragem com isolamento profundo, mutation/race\ne redução medida de alocações/RAM; bytes/pins/waiters têm orçamento por worktree\ne global. Misses coordenadas produzem uma vez por chave; nenhuma contaminação,\nexpansão total desnecessária ou cache de autorização stale. Git reader fica scoped.\n\n### Decision D1\n- Proposal: [Shared domain and optional worktree runtime](../adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md), status Proposed; knowledge:adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review.\n- Basis: R1, R2, R3, R4, R5, R6, R7, R8\n- Decision: Compartilhar somente vistas efetivamente isoladas, com budget em bytes e produção coordenada por chave validada.\n- Rationale: Cópia superficial e contagem de entradas não provam isolamento profundo ou RAM limitada; cada otimização deve preservar grafo e cobertura.\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\n\nFixtures sintéticas e o índice real do repositório como corpus de medição. Os casos V1-V8 foram executados; a evidência de cada requisito está no rastreio e na check `bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration`.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n`go test -race ./internal/pose` nos testes da check acima; a bateria completa de `internal/pose`, `internal/cli` e `internal/mcpserver`; a matriz estrita em clone limpo.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestAViewOfTheGraphDoesNotCopyIt test:TestAViewSeesTheSameGraphEveryTimeAndTheCacheNeverWritesIt check:delivery-integrity-index-compaction-integration\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestADesignDeltaReportSharesNoReferenceWithItsCopies test:TestACachedGraphSharesNoReferenceWithItsCopies test:TestMutatingAReadNeverReachesTheNextRead test:TestDeliveryGraphCopyIsolatesProvenanceMaps test:TestDeliveryGraphCopyIsolatesMaterialInputs test:TestADesignDeltaReportIsIsolatedAndBounded\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestADesignDeltaIsAssessedOncePerKeyAndOnlyACompleteOneIsRetained test:TestTheGraphCacheKeyIsTheContentNotTheSizeOrTheOwner test:TestTheTestCatalogIsKeyedByTheMatrixAndMeteredPerRoot\n- R4 [satisfied] test:TestAPaddedTitleDoesNotKeepItsPaddingAlive test:TestTheOwnersBytesAreChargedToEachEntry test:TestManySmallEntriesAreChargedTheirMetadataToo test:TestACommitWithMorePathsThanTheReaderAcceptsIsUnknownNotClean test:TestASharedResultStaysChargedUntilItsLastWaiterHasCopiedIt test:TestTheTestCatalogDoesNotKeepTheFilesItReadItsNamesFrom test:TestAViewPinsTheEntryAndAnEvictedEntryStaysChargedUntilItLetsGo test:TestTheReservationIsHeldUntilTheResultIsPublished test:TestTheEstimateChargesEveryVariableSizedField test:TestTheDesignDeltaBudgetIsPerWorktree test:TestAValueNotRetainedIsNotCopiedForRetention test:TestProductionsAreAdmittedWithinTheInflightBudget test:TestBoundedCacheEvictsByBytesNotEntries test:TestBoundedCacheHoldsAnOwnerToItsBudget test:TestBoundedCacheDoesNotRetainWhatExceedsTheBudget test:TestRepeatedReadsAreHitsAndAlternationStaysUnderTheBudget test:TestADesignDeltaReportIsIsolatedAndBounded\n- R5 [satisfied] test:TestAPublicationRacingWithCancelledAndLateWaitersKeepsTheCountersExact test:TestAnOverloadedCatalogCacheIsReportedNotTakenForNoCatalog test:TestAQueueOfDistinctKeysIsBounded test:TestACancelledWaiterGivesItsPlaceBack test:TestOverloadIsTheSameRefusalOnEveryConsumer test:TestTheNumberOfProductionsIsCapped test:TestWaitersPerKeyAreCappedAndTheRefusedCallerIsToldToProduceForItself test:TestAReservationLargerThanTheBudgetRunsAloneInsteadOfStarving test:TestACopyDoesNotDelayAnotherKey test:TestADesignDeltaIsAssessedOncePerKeyAndOnlyACompleteOneIsRetained test:TestBoundedCacheProducesOncePerKeyUnderConcurrentMisses test:TestBoundedCacheDoesNotSerializeIndependentKeys test:TestBoundedCacheWaiterCancellationLeavesTheProducerAndOthers test:TestBoundedCacheDoesNotRememberAFailure test:TestConcurrentMissesOnTheSameIndexParseItOnce\n- R6 [satisfied] test:TestTheTestCatalogIsKeyedByTheMatrixAndMeteredPerRoot test:TestBoundedCacheExpiresByTTL\n- R7 [satisfied] test:TestGraphByteEstimateTracksTheMeasuredHeap test:TestTheCostOfDeepIsolationIsMeasured test:TestAViewOfTheGraphDoesNotCopyIt test:TestRepeatedReadsAreHitsAndAlternationStaysUnderTheBudget\n- R8 [satisfied] test:TestBoundedCacheSurvivesAlternatingOwnersUnderRace test:TestACancelledWaiterOnAGraphParseDoesNotAbandonTheOthers check:bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration\n\n### Known gaps\n- Measured on the real index (10.9 MB, 6,937 nodes), heap and allocation only, one machine, one corpus, `go test` timings of single runs (no percentile is claimed): the first parse takes 190 ms and a hit through the deep copy 11.5 ms; the deep copy allocates 18.5 MB where the shallow copy it replaces allocated 5.7 MB (7.2 ms against 1.0 ms), which is the price of isolation; a read of one scope's digest through the view allocates 30 KB against 18.5 MB through the copy (4.2 ms against 11.2 ms, most of it hashing the index bytes for the key). Twelve concurrent first reads produce one parse (274 ms wall, eleven waiters coalesced). The retained size is estimated at 54 MB against 23 MB measured heap (walking every field), an estimate that errs high on purpose. RSS was not measured and no speedup of a whole command is claimed.\n- Only two read-only consumers were moved to the view; the other callers of `GetDeliveryIntegrity` keep the deep copy.\n- The view's contract (do not modify or keep the graph) is documented and tested on the cache side, not enforced by the compiler.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\nOne bounded cache (bytes, global and per worktree, least recently used, optional expiry) carries the parsed delivery graph, the design-delta report and the test catalog; the paths of a commit are read by the governed capture, bounded in output (4 MiB) and in paths (100,000) and not cached, because every governed read is audited. A missed key is produced once however many callers ask, after reserving the bytes it expects to hold against global and per-worktree in-flight budgets, with a cap on productions and on waiters per key; a waiter that leaves does not disturb the producer or the others; a failure is never remembered; a value over its budget, or declared unretainable, is served and neither retained nor copied for retention; copies run outside the lock. Parsed graphs are keyed by engine, schema and the digest of the bytes, so identical bytes share an entry and nothing is served another worktree's graph. The test catalog is keyed by root and the digest of the validation matrix and expires after 30 seconds. The deep isolation is structural: a reflection test fills every slice, map and pointer of the graph and finds the references a copy shares with the original, which reproduced the aliasing the audit had not reproduced (the node attribute maps and the roadmap criteria refs) and fixed it. Read-only consumers can view the graph without a copy (`ViewDeliveryIntegrity`). Left out: moving every consumer to the view, RSS measurement, any persistent or cross-process cache, any global Git pool.\n\n### Files and modules changed\n- pose-mcp/internal/pose (bounded_cache.go, delivery_integrity_cache.go, delivery_integrity.go, delegated_verdicts.go, design_delta.go, test_catalog.go, git_spawn_cache.go and their tests)\n- ADR shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime (amendment); the validation matrix gains `bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration`\n\n### Validation executed\n- Command: `pose validate --strict --jobs 4` on a clean clone of the reviewed head, and the suites of `internal/pose`, `internal/cli` and `internal/mcpserver`\n- Result: recorded by the sealed validation evidence; independent delegated review by a different vendor, concluded with `pose review conclude`.\n\n### Residual risks\n- The clone a caller keeps is the caller's memory and is outside the budget; the view exists for readers that keep nothing. So are the inputs a caller read before asking the cache (the raw index bytes a waiter holds) and the clone being made for a caller: the cache charges what it keeps alive for itself, retained entries, productions, shared results until their last waiter copied them, and pinned entries. Bounding what callers allocate before and after the call is not done here; reading a smaller input is the follow-up below.\n- An overloaded catalog cache is reported: lint-spec and the closeout gate fail with \"test references could not be verified\" instead of treating the missing catalog as an empty one; callers that only skip resolution keep the lenient form.\n- A consumer that needs a mutable graph pays about 7 ms and 18 MB per read; moving more consumers to the view lowers it.\n- The estimate of retained bytes errs high, so the cache holds less than its budget in practice.\n- The 30-second expiry of the test catalog is a policy, not a proof of freshness; gates read the matrix digest in the key.\n\n### Follow-ups\n\n- [open] Move the remaining read-only consumers of the delivery graph to `ViewDeliveryIntegrity` and measure the allocation saved per command. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-01-08)\n- [open] Replace the fixed reservations of the catalog (4 MiB), the design delta (8 MiB) and the graph (a multiple of the raw size) by ceilings enforced on what they read, as the governed commit-paths read already is (4 MiB of Git output and 100,000 paths). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2027-01-08)\n- [open] Bound what callers hold around the cache: read the delivery index in a bounded stream or by a size-gated admission before the bytes are allocated, and reserve the bytes of the clone a caller is about to receive. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2027-01-08)\n- [open] Measure RSS and the retained heap of a long-lived MCP server that alternates between projects, to settle the budgets from more than one corpus. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-01-08)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/bounded_cache.go:334:\t\t\t\tpanic(r)\n\t// reservation are decided together. A value that is not retained is cloned only\n\t// when someone waits for it; a waiter that joins while the copy is being made\n\t// (outside the lock, so that independent keys are never delayed by it) is seen\n\t// when the lock is taken again, and the copy is made for it too.\n\tvar shared V\n\thave := false\n\tfor {\n\t\tif !have && retain {\n\t\t\tshared, have = c.doClone(value), true\n\t\t}\n\t\tc.mu.Lock()\n\t\tif !have && flight.waiters > 0 {\n\t\t\tc.mu.Unlock()\n\t\t\tshared, have = c.doClone(value), true\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tbreak\n\t}\n\tif retain {\n\t\tc.storeLocked(owner, key, shared, size)\n\t}\n\tif flight.waiters > 0 {\n\t\tflight.value, flight.ok = shared, true\n\t\tflight.held = reserve // charged until the last waiter has copied the result\n\t}\n\tflight.finished = true\n\tflight.holders = flight.waiters\n\tc.removeFlightLocked(key, flight)\n\tif flight.holders == 0 {\n\t\tc.releaseLocked(owner, reserve)\n\t}\n\tc.mu.Unlock()\n\tclose(flight.done)\n\treturn value, nil\n}\n\n\tvar graph DeliveryIntegrityGraph\n\tpopulate(reflect.ValueOf(&graph).Elem(), 0)\n\tcopied := copyDeliveryIntegrityGraph(graph)\n\tif !reflect.DeepEqual(graph, copied) {\n\t\tt.Fatal(\"the copy does not equal the original\")\n\t}\n\tif shared := sharedReferences(graph, copied); len(shared) != 0 {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the copy shares %d references with the original:\\n%v\", len(shared), shared)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestMutatingAReadNeverReachesTheNextRead(t *testing.T) {\n\tdeliveryGraphCache.Reset()\n\traw := []byte(`{\"schema_version\":1,\"input_digest\":\"d\",\"nodes\":[{\"id\":\"n\",\"type\":\"t\",\"attributes\":{\"k\":\"v\"}}],\"edges\":[],\"claims\":[],\"change_sets\":[],\"reverse\":{\"p\":[\"a\"]},\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"f\",\"path\":\"p\"}]}`)\n\tfirst, ok := parseDeliveryIntegrityGraph(\"root\", raw)\n\tif !ok {\n\t\tt.Fatal(\"parse failed\")\n\t}\n\tfirst.Nodes[0].Attributes[\"k\"] = \"mutated\"\n\tfirst.Nodes[0].Attributes[\"new\"] = \"x\"\n\tfirst.Reverse[\"p\"][0] = \"mutated\"\n\tfirst.Findings[0].Path = \"mutated\"\n\tfirst.Nodes = first.Nodes[:0]\n\tsecond, ok := parseDeliveryIntegrityGraph(\"root\", raw)\n\tif !ok || len(second.Nodes) != 1 || second.Nodes[0].Attributes[\"k\"] != \"v\" || len(second.Nodes[0].Attributes) != 1 ||\n\t\tsecond.Reverse[\"p\"][0] != \"a\" || second.Findings[0].Path != \"p\" {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a caller's write reached the next read: %+v\", second)\n\t}\n}\n\t\t})\n\t})\n\t_ = sink\n\tt.Logf(\"operation=one scope's provenance digest from a hit: through the deep copy %v / %d B allocated; through the view %v / %d B allocated\", copyT, copyA, viewT, viewA)\n\tif viewA*4 > copyA {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the view allocated %d B against %d B for the copy: it is copying\", viewA, copyA)\n\t}\n}\n\n// A view hands out the retained graph itself: the cache must never modify it, and\n// a reader that keeps within the contract sees the same graph on every read.\nfunc TestAViewSeesTheSameGraphEveryTimeAndTheCacheNeverWritesIt(t *testing.T) {\n\tdeliveryGraphCache.Reset()\n\traw := []byte(`{\"schema_version\":1,\"input_digest\":\"d\",\"nodes\":[{\"id\":\"n\",\"type\":\"t\",\"attributes\":{\"k\":\"v\"}}],\"edges\":[],\"claims\":[],\"change_sets\":[],\"reverse\":{\"p\":[\"a\"]},\"findings\":[]}`)\n\tvar first, second string\n\tviewDeliveryIntegrityGraph(\"o\", raw, func(g DeliveryIntegrityGraph) { first = g.Nodes[0].Attributes[\"k\"] + g.Reverse[\"p\"][0] })\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
