{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '80,105p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_plan.go; sed -n '35,72p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_terminal_verification_test.go; git diff --name-status 33648a12..HEAD -- .pose/closeout-plans/spec-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.json; git status --short; sed -n '1,55p' .pose/knowledge/2026-10-14-decision-log-adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review.md\"","aggregated_output":"\t\treturn store.planCloseout(ref)\n\t}, func(plan *CloseoutPlan, metadata *ReadViewMetadata, audit governanceReadViewAudit) {\n\t\tapplyCloseoutPlanReadView(plan, metadata, ref, audit)\n\t})\n}\n\nfunc applyCloseoutPlanReadView(plan *CloseoutPlan, metadata *ReadViewMetadata, scope string, audit governanceReadViewAudit) {\n\tif metadata == nil {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tcopy := *metadata\n\tcopy.Scope = scope\n\tplan.ReadView = &copy\n\tif plan.Verification != nil {\n\t\tapplyCloseoutReadView(plan.Verification, metadata, scope, audit)\n\t}\n\tif copy.Freshness == ReadViewFreshnessCurrent {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tif plan.LifecycleDone && plan.Terminal && !governanceReviewAuditChanged(audit) &&\n\t\t(plan.Verification == nil || plan.Verification.Terminal) {\n\t\t// The plan is verification-only for a completed scope. Retain its\n\t\t// historical terminal result with the unknown view attached; no step can\n\t\t// use it to perform a new transition.\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\troot, store := terminalVerificationFixture(t, created, policy)\n\t\t\tif tc == \"valid-attempt\" {\n\t\t\t\trecordApprovedReview(t, store, \"rvw-valid\", \"spec:alpha\", \"spec-closeout@1\", \"correctness\", \"\")\n\t\t\t\tpath := filepath.Join(root, \".pose/reviews/rvw-valid.md\")\n\t\t\t\traw, _ := os.ReadFile(path)\n\t\t\t\twriteReviewFixture(t, root, \".pose/reviews/rvw-valid.md\", strings.Replace(string(raw), \"2026-08-02T12:00:00Z\", \"2026-10-24T12:00:00Z\", 1))\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif tc == \"malformed-policy\" {\n\t\t\t\twriteReviewFixture(t, root, \".pose/policy/review.json\", \"{\")\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif tc == \"corrupt-history\" {\n\t\t\t\twriteReviewFixture(t, root, \".pose/specs/alpha.amendments.jsonl\", \"{broken\\n\")\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tstate, stateErr := store.GetCloseoutState(\"spec:alpha\")\n\t\t\tplan, planErr := store.PlanCloseout(\"spec:alpha\")\n\t\t\tif tc == \"malformed-policy\" {\n\t\t\t\tif stateErr == nil || planErr == nil {\n\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unknown certified: %v %v\", stateErr, planErr)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif stateErr != nil || planErr != nil {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"state %v plan %v\", stateErr, planErr)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\twant := tc == \"legacy-cutoff\" || tc == \"policy-off\" || tc == \"valid-attempt\"\n\t\t\tif state.Terminal != want || plan.Terminal != state.Terminal || !plan.LifecycleDone || plan.Verification == nil || !reflect.DeepEqual(plan.Blockers, state.Blockers) {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parity: state=%+v plan=%+v\", state, plan)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tfor _, step := range plan.Steps {\n\t\t\t\tif step.ID == CloseoutStepEvidence || step.ID == CloseoutStepJudgment {\n\t\t\t\t\tif step.State != CloseoutStateNotRun {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"fabricated execution %+v\", step)\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif !want {\n\t\t\t\tnext, ok := plan.NextCloseoutStep()\nD\t.pose/closeout-plans/spec-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.json\n---\ntype: decision-log\nslug: adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review\nowner: @pose-maintainers\nsensitivity: public-internal\ncreated_at: 2026-10-14\nlast_reviewed_at: 2026-10-14\nexpires_at: 2027-01-12\nsource_refs:\n  spec: \"pose-consolidation-batch-14-authoring\"\n  workflow: \"documentation-update\"\n  commands: [\"pose lint-spec pose-consolidation-batch-14-authoring --strict\"]\n  external_sources: []  # [{url: \"\", accessed_at: \"YYYY-MM-DD\"}]\n---\n\n# decision-log: adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review\n\n## Context\n\nReview the [domain/runtime proposal](../adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md)\nfor B31/B33/B35 before functional start, preserving the accepted trust, disclosure\nand scoped-reader boundaries.\n\n## Current state\n\nLast reviewed: 2026-10-14. Proposal is Proposed; specs draft, no IPC/cache/runtime\nor adoption implemented. TTL of 90 days covers staged documentary authoring and\nthe contract review before functional execution; reassess when design/scope changes.\nThe durable rationale stays in the ADR, not in this expiring operational note.\n\n## Next checks\n\nResolve interface/envelope/version compatibility, route/producer inventory, local\nIPC identity/permissions/platforms, cache accounting/view ownership and measured\nQoS thresholds. Execute planned mutation/race/parity/attach/fallback cases only\nwhen the implementation scope is authorized. Lint/merge do not qualify runtime.\n\n## Risks\n\nShared mutable fields can contaminate reads; entry counts do not bound RAM. MCP\nstdio/UID/cache hits are not authority; watch hints are not current generation.\nAmbiguous effects cannot be retried in fallback without receipt/reconciliation.\n\n## Next owner\n\n@pose-maintainers under the existing contract authority, without a new universal\nhuman confirmation or default runtime adoption.\n\n## References\n\n- [Authoring spec](../specs/2026-10-14-pose-consolidation-batch-14-authoring.md)\n- [B31](../specs/2026-10-14-pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff.md)\n- [B33](../specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md)\n- [B35](../specs/2026-10-14-pose-optional-worktree-runtime.md)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
