{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"**Approved for the reviewed change. No open findings.**\n\nThe rebuilt checkout omits the failed checkpoint and matches the approved implementation. Artifact-check, design assessment, and surface-check passed. The test rerun was blocked by the read-only filesystem; functional conclusions use the sealed evidence.\n\n**Terminal closeout remains unverified:** current review/closeout checks report unknown governance freshness and no current approval. Those completion gates must be rerun after POSE records this review.\n\nApplied the POSE review workflow and backend-go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. `SD-64016923` maps to D1 and R1–R8 through the ADR’s ownership, accounting, isolation, coordination, freshness, and measurement decisions. No repository changes or attestation were made.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"prior_findings\": [],\n  \"sweep\": \"The formal previous-round ledger contains no carried findings. Rechecked the failed-checkpoint issue described in the implementer note: HEAD is 5a6714a3, the checkpoint is neither tracked nor present, and comparison with 33648a12 confirms its removal. Verified no implementation, runtime-documentation, ADR or validation-matrix changes since approved head eacc0075. Reviewed cache accounting, isolation, keys, admission, publication, cancellation, error propagation and governed Git bounds against the unchanged requirements and tests. Checked lifecycle and derived/review changes. Artifact, design and surface checks passed. The race-test rerun was blocked before execution by the read-only filesystem. Current terminal verification remains deferred and is not claimed successful.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-b86d2cec5368a46f\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified implementation identity and checkpoint absence independently. Distinguished sealed functional evidence from the blocked test rerun and unsuccessful current terminal diagnostics. Caller-memory exclusions, estimated reservations, catalog freshness and unmeasured RSS remain explicit limits.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The unchanged implementation retains sealed race coverage for admission, publication, cancellation, pinned entries and shared-result reservation lifetime. No fresh test pass is claimed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Defensive-copy contracts, additive views, catalog overload propagation and unknown oversized commit inventories remain unchanged.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Bounded admission, cancellation and production failure paths retain relevant negative coverage. Failures are not cached as successful absence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Production consumers are unchanged. Current strict surface-check passed with one target, 191 results and zero findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Cache counters and bounded overload/incomplete-verification errors remain available. Current governance uncertainty is explicitly reported.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integrity-index-compaction-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"No source or format changes since approval. Legacy and compact decoding and mutable consumer contracts remain supported.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Implementation and validation matrix match the approved head. Relevant build, unit and integration evidence remains sealed; the failed checkpoint is absent from this rebuilt checkout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-b86d2cec5368a46f\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deep copies remove nested aliasing, views reduce whole-graph copying for small reads, byte accounting limits retention and per-key coordination removes duplicate production.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-64016923\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The ADR amendment addresses R1-R8 through explicit ownership, budgets, content keys, isolation, coordination, freshness and measurement boundaries.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Runtime documentation remains consistent with the unchanged implementation. The contradictory failed checkpoint is absent. Lifecycle done is not treated as proof of terminal closeout; final completion verification remains pending.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Overload and unknown coverage remain actionable. Current completion diagnostics require verification of governance inputs before closeout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R1-R8 and the milestone's functional exit conditions retain relevant evidence for the unchanged implementation within the spec's accepted limits. This judgment does not certify administrative terminal closeout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-b86d2cec5368a46f\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Git confirms only lifecycle and derived/review changes since approval. No additional functional scope was introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-and-dispatch-snapshot-integrity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"No authority cache or shared Git pool was introduced. Unproven governance inputs continue to prevent successful terminal verification.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-b86d2cec5368a46f\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reusable cache implementation and limited view migration address the observed causes. Entry-count limits or shallow copies would be insufficient. Broader residency, new mutable dependencies or changed ownership would require reconsideration.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"check:pose artifact-check --spec pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed successfully, exit 0, with provenance warnings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-b86d2cec5368a46f\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed successfully. Structural input and implementation digests match the sealed evidence and approved implementation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Avoided repository-writing assessment refresh under the no-change boundary. Inspected the component and verified unchanged sources directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Avoided repository-writing assessment refresh. Used unchanged consumer inspection, sealed integration evidence and the current successful surface check.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Avoided repository-writing assessment refresh. Direct marker inspection found the intentional producer panic cleanup/rethrow. Reservation, caller-memory and measurement debt remains documented with owned follow-ups.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion-only gate. Diagnostic invocation exited 1 with lifecycle_done=true, review_approved=false, terminal=false and unknown governance freshness. It must be rerun after POSE records the review and verifies current inputs. No successful terminal closeout is claimed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion-only gate. Diagnostic invocation exited 1 with no current review attempt and unknown governance freshness. Final freshness and approval verification belongs after POSE records this conclusion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"check:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed successfully and applied the selected review workflow and rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed strict surface-check: exit 0, one target, 191 results, zero findings. Supporting sealed reachability evidence: reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reused sealed validation for the verified unchanged implementation. Supporting classes: unit:pose-mcp/go/test; integration:pose-mcp/go/bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration; e2e:pose-mcp/go/multi-repo-agent-installed-journey. The registered race-test rerun was blocked before execution because Go could not create its work directory on the read-only filesystem.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reused sealed module validation after verifying no source or validation-matrix changes since approval. Supporting classes: build:pose-mcp/go/build; unit:pose-mcp/go/test; e2e:pose-mcp/go/multi-repo-agent-installed-journey. No fresh test pass is claimed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
